# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your real values there.
# ".env" is gitignored — it never gets committed or shared. This ".env.example"
# has NO real secrets; it just documents which names your agent expects.
#
# In .mcp.json, these are referenced as ${SLACK_BOT_TOKEN}, ${MONDAY_API_TOKEN}, etc.,
# so the real values stay only in your local .env.
#
# /build-agent adds the lines you actually need. Delete the ones you don't.

# --- Google stack (if used) ---
# Most Google/Slack/Microsoft connectors sign in through a browser pop-up (OAuth)
# instead of a token you paste here. Leave those blank — you'll be prompted to log in.

# --- Token-based connectors (examples) ---
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
# MONDAY_API_TOKEN=
# QUICKBOOKS_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# CRELATE_API_KEY=
